 - For numerical, data, or media work, reconcile units, coordinate transforms, axis direction, indexing origin, and inclusive or exclusive bounds before implementing. Validate every stated numerical constraint using the same definition and units exposed through the required public output.
+- For numerical fitting or estimation, define the requested model and parameter conventions before optimizing. Report parameters from that model; use richer nuisance terms only as sensitivity checks unless the task explicitly asks for them, and check stability across reasonable fitting choices before finalizing.
 - For long searches, builds, training, solvers, benchmarks, or experiments, use a bounded anytime plan. As soon as a valid or best-so-far candidate appears, persist it to the required output path; reserve time for exact acceptance validation rather than leaving the only good result in transient output.
 - Before finishing, run an independent evaluator-facing semantic check through the exact public interface and expected working directory. Build success, imports, syntax checks, and file existence alone are not sufficient; when hidden inputs are implied, exercise at least one relevant boundary case. If stale output or an existing process could satisfy the check, reproduce the result from a fresh disposable state before preserving the newly verified publish state.
 - Once an evaluator-shaped check passes, treat that filesystem and service state as the publish state. Do not reset a repository, stop a required service, or delete or rewrite required outputs merely to make the workspace look clean. Remove only explicitly forbidden extras, then rerun the same check.
